# Error Handling & Logging

## Typed errors

Flow: catch at repository → `Either<Failure, T>` → fold in Cubit → UI state.

- Use cases return `Future<Either<Failure, T>>` via `UseCase<T, Param>`.
- Repositories wrap risky work with `safeCall` (`lib/core/utils/safe_call.dart`).
- `safeCall` maps: `DioException` → `failureFromDioException`; `FormatException` → `ServerFailure`; other → `ServerFailure`.

## Failure types (`lib/core/errors/failures.dart`)

`ServerFailure`, `NetworkFailure`, `CacheFailure` / `CacheNotFoundFailure`, `AuthFailure` / `TokenExpiredFailure` / `UnauthorizedFailure`, `ValidationFailure` (optional `fieldErrors`).

Prefer existing types; extend the hierarchy only when a new domain category is needed.

## Layers

| Layer | Role |
|-------|------|
| Technical | Dio/Hive exceptions caught in `safeCall` / data sources |
| Domain | `Failure` messages — user-safe, no secrets |
| UI | `*Error(message)` + Retry; empty via dedicated widgets |

## Logging

- Use `Logger` from `lib/core/utils/logger.dart`.
- Never log tokens, API keys, passwords, or PII.
- Network logging interceptor is for debug — do not log auth headers with secrets.

## Theme exception

`ThemeCubit` uses try/catch + emit (no Either). Keep that local to preference features; API features must use Either.
